{
  "title": "Quilt",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Everything that can",
        "be played gently: 38",
        "instruments, all",
        "synthesised, none",
        "sampled.",
        "",
        "Felt pianos,",
        "electric pianos,",
        "organs, mallets and",
        "bells, harp and",
        "guitar, bowed",
        "strings, glass,",
        "flutes and a choir.",
        "",
        "Each one is a model",
        "of the real thing:",
        "something soft meets",
        "something that",
        "rings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Getting started",
      "lines": [
        "Put Quilt in a synth",
        "slot and play the",
        "pads.",
        "",
        "Turn TYPE to choose",
        "an instrument. It",
        "arrives with its own",
        "sound on every page,",
        "ready to play. Only",
        "VOL stays where you",
        "left it.",
        "",
        "Or jog the presets",
        "on the Main page:",
        "three for each",
        "instrument, 114 in",
        "all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Playing",
      "lines": [
        "Velocity is how hard",
        "the hammer, mallet,",
        "finger or bow meets",
        "the instrument.",
        "",
        "Pressure matters on",
        "the bowed, blown and",
        "sung instruments:",
        "press harder to bow",
        "or breathe harder,",
        "and the note swells.",
        "",
        "With no pressure, as",
        "from a keyboard,",
        "they swell by",
        "themselves. PRESS on",
        "the Instrument page",
        "picks Pad, Auto or",
        "Blend.",
        "",
        "The mod wheel adds",
        "vibrato to the",
        "bowed, blown and",
        "sung instruments,",
        "and spins up the",
        "organ's Leslie. A",
        "sustain pedal lifts",
        "the dampers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Presets",
      "lines": [
        "Each instrument has",
        "three presets. The",
        "first is its own",
        "default sound, the",
        "one TYPE loads.",
        "",
        "The list runs A to Z",
        "by instrument.",
        "",
        "The other two are",
        "familiar ways to",
        "play it: a muted",
        "chime, a cello that",
        "bows by itself, an",
        "organ with",
        "percussion.",
        "",
        "Every preset plays",
        "at the same",
        "loudness, so you can",
        "browse without",
        "reaching for VOL.",
        "",
        "Auto presets hold",
        "notes steady however",
        "hard you press."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pages",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Main",
          "lines": [
            "TYPE",
            " The instrument,",
            " with its whole",
            " default sound.",
            "",
            "SOFT",
            " Softer hammer,",
            " mallet, finger, bow",
            " or breath. On the",
            " organ, fewer bright",
            " drawbars.",
            "",
            "CHAR",
            " Each instrument's",
            " own control. Its",
            " name changes with",
            " TYPE: FELT, VEIL,",
            " PUFF. See",
            " Instruments.",
            "",
            "DECAY",
            " How long notes",
            " ring, or how slowly",
            " they fade after you",
            " let go.",
            "",
            "SWAY",
            " Motion: auto-pan,",
            " tremolo, vibrato,",
            " or the Leslie from",
            " slow to fast.",
            "",
            "TONE",
            " Darker to brighter.",
            " The middle is flat.",
            "",
            "SPACE",
            " How much reverb.",
            "",
            "VOL",
            " Output level."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Instrument",
          "lines": [
            "Named after the",
            "instrument you are",
            "playing. Its knobs",
            "depend on the kind",
            "of instrument:",
            "",
            "Keys and mallets:",
            " SPLIT STIFF SPOT",
            " BODY NOISE DAMP",
            " PEDAL",
            "",
            "Plucked:",
            " SPOT BODY EDGE",
            " NOISE DAMP STIFF",
            "",
            "Bowed:",
            " BODY EDGE PRESS",
            " SWELL NOISE BITE",
            "",
            "Glass:",
            " BOW BLUR HIT",
            " PRESS SWELL NOISE",
            "",
            "Breath:",
            " ONSET EDGE PRESS",
            " SWELL AIR",
            "",
            "Organ:",
            " PING TAIL CLICK",
            " LEAK SLOW FAST 1'",
            "",
            "Choir:",
            " CROWD AIR SWELL",
            " PRESS SPLIT",
            "",
            "Hold a knob to see",
            "its full name."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Instrument knobs",
          "lines": [
            "SPLIT",
            " Strings or voices",
            " of a note drift",
            " apart.",
            "",
            "STIFF",
            " Stiffer strings:",
            " overtones stretch",
            " sharp.",
            "",
            "SPOT",
            " Strike or pluck",
            " nearer the end:",
            " brighter.",
            "",
            "BODY",
            " More soundboard or",
            " body.",
            "",
            "NOISE",
            " Key, finger, bow or",
            " friction noise.",
            "",
            "DAMP",
            " Notes stop faster",
            " when let go.",
            "",
            "PEDAL",
            " Sustain pedal down.",
            "",
            "EDGE",
            " A brighter string,",
            " pipe or rank.",
            "",
            "PRESS",
            " What sets a held",
            " note's level: Pad",
            " pressure, Auto",
            " swell, or a Blend.",
            "",
            "SWELL",
            " Slower swell and",
            " attack.",
            "",
            "BITE",
            " The bow grips",
            " harder at the",
            " start.",
            "",
            "BOW",
            " A faster bow.",
            "",
            "BLUR",
            " A less pure tone.",
            "",
            "HIT",
            " A mallet strike",
            " under the bow.",
            "",
            "ONSET",
            " A firmer start, as",
            " tonguing.",
            "",
            "AIR",
            " More breath.",
            "",
            "CROWD",
            " One, two or three",
            " singers per note.",
            "",
            "TUNE TINE",
            " The glass e.piano's",
            " bell tuning and",
            " tine depth.",
            "",
            "8' 4' 2'",
            " The flute organ's",
            " and string",
            " ensemble's",
            " registers."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Organ",
          "lines": [
            "The tonewheel organ",
            "has nine drawbars:",
            "1' on the Instrument",
            "page, the other",
            "eight on the",
            "Drawbars page.",
            "",
            "They run in the",
            "real organ's order:",
            "16' and 5 1/3' are",
            "the low subs, 8' is",
            "the note itself,",
            "then up through the",
            "harmonics. So",
            "drawbar settings",
            "like 888000000 read",
            "straight across.",
            "",
            "PING adds the",
            "percussion on the",
            "third harmonic and",
            "TAIL sets how long",
            "it lasts. CLICK is",
            "the key contacts,",
            "LEAK the",
            "neighbouring wheels.",
            "",
            "SWAY moves the",
            "Leslie between SLOW",
            "and FAST, and it",
            "speeds up and slows",
            "down like a real",
            "rotor."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Effects",
          "lines": [
            "SIZE",
            " A larger reverb.",
            "",
            "DARK",
            " A darker reverb.",
            "",
            "DELAY",
            " A longer gap before",
            " the reverb.",
            "",
            "DRIVE",
            " Gentle warmth, as",
            " from an amplifier.",
            "",
            "SPEED",
            " How fast SWAY",
            " moves. Not on the",
            " vibraphone or",
            " organ, which have",
            " their own."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Modulation",
          "lines": [
            "MOD",
            "  Which of the four",
            "  modulators.",
            "",
            "KIND",
            "  What it follows:",
            "  Velocity, MPE, LFO",
            "  or Envelope.",
            "",
            "SHAPE, RATE",
            "  The LFO's wave and",
            "  speed. Right of",
            "  centre: in time,",
            "  8 bars to 1/64.",
            "  Left: free, slow",
            "  to fast.",
            "",
            "RISE, FALL",
            "  The envelope: up",
            "  while held, down",
            "  after.",
            "",
            "AXIS, LAG",
            "  MPE pressure,",
            "  slide or bend, and",
            "  its smoothing.",
            "",
            "AIM, DEPTH",
            "  Two destinations:",
            "  TONE, SOFT, CHAR,",
            "  DECAY, SWAY,",
            "  SPACE, VOL, TYPE,",
            "  or the",
            "  next modulator's",
            "  rate or depth.",
            "  DEPTH goes either",
            "  way.",
            "",
            "  Presets leave this",
            "  page alone."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Instruments",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Keys and organs",
          "lines": [
            "Felt Upright",
            " FELT: the felt",
            " strip between",
            " hammer and string",
            "",
            "Una Corda Grand",
            " HUSH: the soft",
            " pedal, two strings",
            " not three",
            "",
            "Electric Grand",
            " TWANG: the pickups",
            " move toward the",
            " bridge",
            "",
            "Clavichord",
            " BEND: press a held",
            " pad and the note",
            " wavers",
            "",
            "Tine Piano",
            " BARK: tines voiced",
            " toward the pickup",
            "",
            "Reed Piano",
            " BITE: the pickup",
            " gap narrows",
            "",
            "Celesta",
            " BELL: more of the",
            " bell overtones",
            "",
            "Toy Piano",
            " BELL: more of the",
            " bell overtones",
            "",
            "Tonewheel Organ",
            " LUSH: the scanner",
            " chorus. Drawbars on",
            " their own page",
            "",
            "Flute Organ",
            " PUFF: the chiff at",
            " the start of a pipe",
            "",
            "Harmonium",
            " BEAT: the celeste",
            " rank beating",
            "",
            "Glass E.Piano",
            " GLASS: the glassy",
            " bell",
            "",
            "String Ensemble",
            " LUSH: the ensemble",
            " chorus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Mallets and bells",
          "lines": [
            "Vibraphone",
            " MOTOR: fan speed.",
            " SWAY is its depth",
            "",
            "Marimba",
            " ROLL: hold a pad",
            " and the mallets",
            " roll; press to roll",
            " faster",
            "",
            "Xylophone",
            " ROLL: as the",
            " marimba",
            "",
            "Glockenspiel",
            " BELL: more of the",
            " bell overtones",
            "",
            "Tubular Bells",
            " MUTE: a hand on the",
            " tube",
            "",
            "Handbells",
            " MINOR: the minor",
            " third in the bell",
            "",
            "Handpan",
            " RING: the harmonic",
            " ring",
            "",
            "Tongue Drum",
            " RING: the harmonic",
            " ring",
            "",
            "Kalimba / Music Box",
            " BUZZ: the buzzers.",
            " At zero it is a",
            " music box"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Strings",
          "lines": [
            "Harp",
            " BLOOM: the other",
            " strings ring along",
            "",
            "Nylon Guitar",
            " BLOOM: the open",
            " strings ring along",
            "",
            "Hammered Dulcimer",
            " BLOOM: the undamped",
            " strings ring along",
            "",
            "Pizzicato",
            " DEEP: from violas",
            " to cellos",
            "",
            "Solo Cello",
            " VEIL: the bow moves",
            " over the",
            " fingerboard",
            "",
            "Solo Violin",
            " VEIL: the bow moves",
            " over the",
            " fingerboard",
            "",
            "String Section",
            " WIDTH: the players",
            " spread apart"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Glass and bowls",
          "lines": [
            "Bowed Vibes",
            " GRIP: the bow grips",
            " harder",
            "",
            "Glass Harmonica",
            " WET: a wetter",
            " finger, smoother",
            "",
            "Singing Bowl",
            " BEAT: the bowl's",
            " pairs beat"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Breath and voice",
          "lines": [
            "Flute",
            " COVER: the lip",
            " covers more of the",
            " hole",
            "",
            "Pan Flute",
            " PUFF: the chiff",
            "",
            "Ocarina",
            " PURE: a purer tone",
            "",
            "Recorder",
            " PUFF: the chiff",
            "",
            "Clarinet",
            " REED: a stiffer",
            " reed",
            "",
            "Choir",
            " VOWEL: from oo",
            " through oh to ah"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tips",
      "lines": [
        "For a keyboard",
        "without pressure,",
        "choose an Auto",
        "preset, or set PRESS",
        "to Auto.",
        "",
        "A saved set keeps",
        "your sound exactly;",
        "turning TYPE away",
        "and back brings the",
        "default sound again.",
        "",
        "Quilt plays up to 16",
        "notes at once."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
